$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'wall {"points": [[0,0],[6000,0],[6000,4000],[0,4000]], "closed": true, "type": "Exterior - 300mm"}' --cmd 'camera {"eye": [1000, 1000, 1000], "target": [1000, 1000, 1000]}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout
{"ids":[100002,100003,100004,100005]}

--- stderr
line 1 (camera): camera: the eye is on the target; give the camera two points a little apart

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'wall {"points": [[0,0],[6000,0],[6000,4000],[0,4000]], "closed": true, "type": "Exterior - 300mm"}' --cmd 'camera {"eye": [0, 0, 1000], "target": [1000, 1000, 1000], "lens": 5}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout
{"ids":[100002,100003,100004,100005]}

--- stderr
line 1 (camera): camera: a 5 mm lens is no camera's; a camera's lens is 10 to 600 mm

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'wall {"points": [[0,0],[6000,0],[6000,4000],[0,4000]], "closed": true, "type": "Exterior - 300mm"}' --cmd 'camera {"eye": [0, 0, 1000], "target": [1000, 1000, 1000], "lens": 601}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout
{"ids":[100002,100003,100004,100005]}

--- stderr
line 1 (camera): camera: a 601 mm lens is no camera's; a camera's lens is 10 to 600 mm

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'wall {"points": [[0,0],[6000,0],[6000,4000],[0,4000]], "closed": true, "type": "Exterior - 300mm"}' --cmd 'camera {"eye": [0, 0, 1000]}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout
{"ids":[100002,100003,100004,100005]}

--- stderr
line 1 (camera): camera: `eye` and `target` [x, y, z] are both required to set a camera

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'wall {"points": [[0,0],[6000,0],[6000,4000],[0,4000]], "closed": true, "type": "Exterior - 300mm"}' --cmd 'camera {"view": "Level 1", "lens": 50}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout
{"ids":[100002,100003,100004,100005]}

--- stderr
line 1 (camera): camera: Level 1 isn't a 3D view; a camera goes on a 3D view

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'wall {"points": [[0,0],[6000,0],[6000,4000],[0,4000]], "closed": true, "type": "Exterior - 300mm"}' --cmd 'camera {"eye": [0, 0], "target": [1000, 1000, 1000]}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout
{"ids":[100002,100003,100004,100005]}

--- stderr
line 1 (camera): camera: `eye` must be a point [x, y, z] in mm, got [0,0]

